1: # cTrader + Appwrite: Master-Slave Trading Auth Layer Architecture
2: 
3: ## Overview
4: 
5: This document designs a complete master-slave trading platform where a single master operator controls trade execution across multiple slave cTrader accounts. Appwrite — available free via the GitHub Student Developer Pack — serves as the full backend: hosting the web UI via Sites, handling the OAuth callback via Functions, storing slave tokens and trade configs in Databases, and managing master login via Auth.[^1][^2][^3][^4][^5]
6: 
7: The architecture separates two distinct identities:
8: - **Master**: The operator/developer who runs the platform, logs in with a username + PIN, and controls or monitors all slave accounts.
9: - **Slave**: Any cTrader account holder who grants your app permission once via OAuth, after which your backend can trade their account autonomously.
10: 
11: ***
12: 
