89: 
90: ## Database Schema
91: 
92: All data lives in a single Appwrite Database. Collections are structured as follows:[^2][^10]
93: 
94: ### Collection: `slave_accounts`
95: 
96: Stores the core identity and cTrader token data for each onboarded slave.
97: 
98: | Attribute | Type | Notes |
99: |---|---|---|
100: | `appwrite_user_id` | String | Appwrite Auth UID — document owner |
101: | `username` | String | Chosen display name (unique index) |
102: | `pin_hash` | String | bcrypt hash of 4–6 digit PIN |
103: | `ctrader_access_token` | String | Current short-lived token |
104: | `ctrader_refresh_token` | String | Long-lived, stored server-side only |
105: | `ctrader_account_ids` | String[] | Array of `ctidTraderAccountId` values |
106: | `active` | Boolean | Whether account is currently being traded |
107: | `created_at` | DateTime | ISO timestamp |
108: 
109: **Permissions**: `read("user:<appwrite_user_id>")`, write granted only to server API key via Functions. The slave can read their own record but cannot write `ctrader_refresh_token` directly — only the server-side Function can.[^9]
110: 
111: ### Collection: `trade_configs`
112: 
113: Per-slave trade configuration persisted and editable from the dashboard.
114: 
115: | Attribute | Type | Notes |
116: |---|---|---|
117: | `slave_user_id` | String | FK → `slave_accounts.$id` |
118: | `lot_size` | Float | Default lot size for copied trades |
119: | `lot_multiplier` | Float | Scale factor vs master lot (e.g., 0.5 = half size) |
120: | `max_daily_drawdown_pct` | Float | Kill-switch threshold (%) |
121: | `allowed_symbols` | String[] | Whitelist of symbols to trade (empty = all) |
122: | `copy_enabled` | Boolean | Master kill-switch per slave |
123: | `updated_at` | DateTime | Tracks last config change |
124: 
125: **Permissions**: `read("user:<slave_user_id>")`, `update("user:<slave_user_id>")`, `delete("user:<slave_user_id>")`. Slaves own and can edit their own config. Master uses server SDK (bypasses permissions).[^2]
126: 
127: ### Collection: `master_signals` (Optional)
128: 
129: If building a signal broadcast model rather than direct copy-trading:
130: 
131: | Attribute | Type | Notes |
132: |---|---|---|
133: | `signal_id` | String | Unique ID |
134: | `symbol` | String | e.g., `EURUSD` |
135: | `direction` | Enum | `BUY` / `SELL` |
136: | `lot_size` | Float | Master's base lot |
137: | `sl_pips` | Integer | Stop loss in pips |
138: | `tp_pips` | Integer | Take profit in pips |
139: | `status` | Enum | `PENDING` / `EXECUTED` / `CANCELLED` |
140: | `created_at` | DateTime | Signal broadcast time |
141: 
142: **Permissions**: `read(Role.label("master"))` for create/delete, `read(Role.users("verified"))` for read — all verified slaves can subscribe to signals via Appwrite Realtime.[^3]
