146: ## Complete Auth & Onboarding Flow
147: 
148: ### Step 1: Slave Registration
149: 
150: ```
151: Slave visits Sites URL
152:   → Clicks "Connect cTrader Account"
153:   → Frontend: account.create(ID.unique(), email, password)
154:   → Appwrite creates user → returns userId
155:   → Frontend: calls Function `generate-ctrader-oauth-url`
156:      with { appwrite_userId }
157:   → Function returns:
158:      https://id.ctrader.com/my/settings/openapi/grantingaccess/
159:        ?client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID
160:        &redirect_uri=https://YOUR_FUNCTION_DOMAIN/callback
161:        &scope=trading
162:        &state=<appwrite_userId>   ← ties OAuth result back to Appwrite user
163:   → Slave is redirected to cTrader consent page
164:   → Slave logs in with THEIR cTID and clicks "Allow"
165:   → cTrader redirects to: YOUR_FUNCTION_DOMAIN/callback?code=XXX&state=<userId>
166: ```
167: 
168: ### Step 2: OAuth Callback (Function)
169: 
170: ```
171: Function `ctrader-oauth-callback` receives GET request:
172:   1. Extract code + state (= appwrite_userId)
173:   2. POST to https://id.ctrader.com/Apps/token:
174:        { client_id, client_secret, code, grant_type: "authorization_code",
175:          redirect_uri: FUNCTION_DOMAIN }
176:   3. Receive { access_token, refresh_token, token_type }
177:   4. Connect to cTrader Open API TCP/gRPC:
178:        ProtoOAApplicationAuthReq(clientId, clientSecret)
179:        ProtoOAAccountAuthReq(access_token)
180:        ProtoOAGetAccountListByAccessTokenReq(access_token)
181:   5. Save to DB (server SDK, API key):
182:        databases.createDocument("slave_accounts", {
183:          appwrite_user_id: state,
184:          ctrader_access_token: access_token,
185:          ctrader_refresh_token: refresh_token,
186:          ctrader_account_ids: [...accountIds],
187:          active: false
188:        })
189:   6. Redirect to: SITES_URL/onboarding?success=true
190: ```
191: 
192: ### Step 3: Slave Sets Username + PIN
193: 
194: ```
195: Slave is prompted to choose username + PIN:
196:   → Frontend sends { username, pin } to Function `set-credentials`
197:   → Function:
198:        1. Validates username uniqueness against DB
199:        2. bcrypt.hash(pin, 10) → pin_hash
200:        3. databases.updateDocument("slave_accounts", docId, { username, pin_hash })
201:        4. account.updateName(appwrite_userId, username)  [via server SDK]
202:   → Done — slave now has username + PIN for future logins
203: ```
204: 
205: ### Step 4: Subsequent Slave Login (PIN Auth)
206: 
207: ```
208: Slave visits Sites → enters username + PIN
209:   → Frontend calls Function `pin-login`:
210:        { username, pin }
211:   → Function:
212:        1. Query: databases.listDocuments("slave_accounts",
213:             [Query.equal("username", username)])
214:        2. bcrypt.compare(pin, doc.pin_hash) → valid?
215:        3. If valid: users.createToken(doc.appwrite_user_id)
216:           → returns { secret, userId }
217:   → Frontend receives { secret, userId }
218:   → Frontend: account.createSession({ userId, secret })
219:   → Full Appwrite session established — JWT available
220:   → Slave can now read/write their own trade_configs document
221: ```
222: 
223: ### Step 5: Slave Configures Trade Settings
224: 
225: ```
226: Authenticated slave (has JWT session):
227:   → Frontend calls databases.getDocument("trade_configs", ...)
228:   → Displays: lot_size, lot_multiplier, max_daily_drawdown_pct,
229:               allowed_symbols, copy_enabled
230:   → Slave edits and saves
231:   → Frontend calls databases.updateDocument(...)
232:      (permitted because doc has user-level write permission)
233:   → Changes are persisted immediately to Appwrite DB
234: ```
235: 
236: ### Step 6: Master Reads Configs & Executes Trades
237: 
238: ```
239: Master's backend (running Python/Node on your VPS or Appwrite Function):
240:   1. Queries all slave_accounts where active=true
241:   2. For each slave, refreshes accessToken if needed
242:   3. Reads their trade_config (lot_multiplier, allowed_symbols, etc.)
243:   4. On master signal / trigger:
244:        a. ProtoOAApplicationAuthReq (your app credentials)
245:        b. For each slave:
246:             ProtoOAAccountAuthReq(slave.ctrader_access_token)
247:             ProtoOANewOrderReq(scaled by lot_multiplier)
248:   5. Updates master_signals doc status to EXECUTED
249: ```
