253: ## Security Design Considerations
254: 
255: | Concern | Mitigation |
256: |---|---|
257: | `refresh_token` exposure | Stored only in Appwrite DB server-side; never returned to client SDK; accessible only via API key-authenticated Functions[^2] |
258: | PIN brute force | Appwrite Functions can enforce rate-limiting; lock account after N failures (update `active: false` via server SDK) |
259: | Slave modifying another slave's config | Document-level permissions: each `trade_configs` doc is `write("user:<userId>")` — Appwrite enforces this[^9] |
260: | Master operations from browser | Master uses a separate admin Function endpoint authenticated by a long-lived API key (not a client session) |
261: | cTrader token expiry | Scheduled cron Function handles token refresh before the access token expires[^5] |
262: | Scope creep | OAuth scope set to `trading` — this is the minimum required; avoid storing broker passwords anywhere |
263: 
264: ***
265: 
266: ## Appwrite Function Environment Variables
267: 
268: Store all secrets as Function environment variables (not in DB or code):[^5]
269: 
270: ```
271: CTRADER_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id
272: CTRADER_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret
273: CTRADER_REDIRECT_URI=https://YOUR_FUNCTION_DOMAIN/callback
274: APPWRITE_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id
275: APPWRITE_API_KEY=your_server_api_key
276: APPWRITE_DATABASE_ID=main_db_id
277: BCRYPT_SALT_ROUNDS=10
278: ```
