### 1. Frontend handles browser OAuth

The frontend never touches cTrader secrets. It simply redirects and then polls the session endpoint:

```javascript
// 1. Redirect user to the Worker
window.location.href = "https://auth-ctrader.mrme0.store/auth/ctrader/start?user_id=" + encodeURIComponent(userId);

// 2. After callback redirect, read session (and capture grant_id)
const res = await fetch("https://auth-ctrader.mrme0.store/auth/ctrader/session", {
  credentials: "include",
});
const session = await res.json();
// session = { authenticated: true, user_id: "...", grant_id: "...", expires_at: 1234567890 }

// 3. Send grant_id to your Python backend
await fetch("https://your-backend.example.com/link-ctrader", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({ grant_id: session.grant_id }),
});
```

