### cTrader Auth Broker — Deployment Guide > Architecture > Token Rotation Strategy
### Token Rotation Strategy

cTrader invalidates the previous access/refresh token pair upon every refresh. The broker handles this by:

1. Storing the refresh token encrypted at rest (AES-GCM-256).
2. Routing every refresh operation for a given grant through a single Durable Object instance keyed by `grantId`.
3. Collapsing concurrent refresh requests onto the same in-flight promise inside the DO, ensuring only one cTrader API call executes.
4. Atomically updating D1 with the new encrypted token pair before releasing the DO promise.
5. Purging the KV grant cache after rotation so subsequent reads fetch the new tokens from D1.

A 5-minute safety buffer (`TOKEN_REFRESH_BUFFER_SEC`) triggers proactive refresh before expiry.

